<%# Lab page for the Phantom mobile deep link and the picker gate that depends
    on it.

    TWO STATES ON ONE PAGE, chosen by ?deeplink=1, because the property under
    test is a DIFFERENCE: the engine's wallet picker must collapse its mobile
    Phantom rows only when startPhantomDeepLink actually exists. A page that
    could only render one state could not observe that at all.

    Nothing here reimplements either side. The deep link's browser program lives
    in studio/solana/_phantom_deeplink and the gate lives in the picker's
    x-data; a lab page that hand-rolled either would grade itself.

    tweetnacl is deliberately NOT loaded: blockOffsiteRequests empties the CDN in
    this lane, and none of the assertions need it. Defining the function does not
    require nacl — only calling it does — and the assertions here are about the
    script having parsed and the gate having flipped. %>
<% render_deeplink = params[:deeplink] == "1" %>

<div data-test="deeplink-state" data-deeplink="<%= render_deeplink %>"></div>

<% if render_deeplink %>
  <%= render "studio/solana/phantom_deeplink" %>
<% end %>

<%# The picker, mounted on its own page-scoped store so it needs no app host. %>
<%= render "studio/modals/scoped_host", store: "labModals" do %>
  <template x-if="$store.labModals.current()?.id === 'wallet-connect'">
    <%= render "studio/modals/wallet_connect", store: "labModals" %>
  </template>
<% end %>

<button type="button" data-test="open-picker"
        x-data @click="$store.labModals.open('wallet-connect', {})">Open picker</button>
